{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Independent documentation review: comical-infatuated-motmot\n\n- Reviewer: Codex agent `/root/review_comical_docs` (non-author)\n- Reviewed commit: `c27403e6deb0bee8dfd3db56c74178c76240c552`\n- Exact parent: `665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732`\n- Ticket: `1ab0-d79a-a8f7-459a`\n- Change-Id: `I58689866425034d94b0dbf3465dbdbba500f04ab`\n- Reviewed at: `2026-09-09T15:30:14Z`\n- Verdict: **PASS**\n\n## Method\n\nI verified the worktree's `HEAD` and first parent before and after review. I derived the inventory from the ticket's stable allowlist, then independently compared every allowed block at the exact parent and commit. For each block I read the surrounding implementation and inspected call sites or focused tests where the prose made a cross-module claim. I checked semantic preservation, current accuracy, ownership, retained rationale and constraints, directives, references, stale wording, and condensation loss.\n\nThe 18 authored source and eval-spec paths have unchanged non-prose content. Python sources parse with `type_comments=True`, and their executable ASTs match after removing only the allowlisted leading docstrings. Non-allowlisted full-line comments, every inline comment, directive text, and directive attachment match. The two YAML files have identical non-allowlisted text. The nineteenth path, `docs/env-vars.md`, contains only the generator-owned Bedrock source-line projection.\n\n## Block receipt\n\n| # | Stable block | Verdict | Independent rationale |\n|---:|---|---|---|\n| 01 | `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The summary accurately assigns call-argument preparation and post-call telemetry here, and it preserves the runtime import direction that keeps the LLM package's base import light. |\n| 02 | `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py#D:_memo_toolsets` | PASS | The four-tool allowlist, closure-owned cache and locks, executed-call ledger rule, normalized-path `read_file` cache, exact-signature peers, and pass-through behavior all match the wrapper implementation. |\n| 03 | `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py#C:_memo_toolsets:before:read_cache` | PASS | The comment states the reason for storing whole-file values at the cache definition, and the range-slicing path below uses that representation exactly. |\n| 04 | `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py#D:<module>` | PASS | Provider-qualified resolution, Anthropic construction, loopback bypass ownership, capability separation, lazy heavy imports, and the one-way runner dependency remain explicit and accurate. |\n| 05 | `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py#D:_build_retry_wait` | PASS | The text matches the positive `Retry-After` path and the equal-jitter fallback for missing, expired, or non-positive values, including the bounded cap and injectable RNG. |\n| 06 | `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py#D:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider` | PASS | Transport-only retries, disabled SDK retries, below-agent retry placement, bounded timeouts, loopback endpoint handling, fail-closed supplied auth, ambient fallback only when auth is absent, and caller-owned close are preserved. |\n| 07 | `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The condensed module contract retains the inference-profile requirement, ambient AWS authentication, lazy Bedrock imports, and lack of a runtime dependency on `runner`. |\n| 08 | `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py#D:resolve_bedrock_region` | PASS | The documented precedence matches the loop exactly, including configured-source retention, empty-value treatment, explicit `AWS_REGION` support, and the `(None, None)` boto3-profile fallback. |\n| 09 | `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py#D:build_bedrock_provider` | PASS | The bare-provider contract, local boto3 client construction, adaptive total-attempt mapping, connect/read timeout mapping, deliberate lack of a max-wait mapping, explicit region, ambient credentials, and no teardown registration all match the body. |\n| 10 | `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py#C:build_bedrock_provider:before:raise LLMConfigError` | PASS | The comment precisely explains the guard's purpose: replace boto3's missing-region failure with the typed configuration error without inventing a region. |\n| 11 | `src/rebar/llm/build_drift.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The warning remains correctly described as ancestry-proven and advisory, with fail-open behavior for missing or unrelated Git evidence and downward notification into core config. |\n| 12 | `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The module summary retains warning-only ownership, marked-prefix estimation, the inbound caller direction, and the absence of runner or provider-heavy imports. |\n| 13 | `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py#D:warn_if_cache_ineffective` | PASS | The nonzero-billing prerequisite, model-specific floor, known-prefix two-arm diagnosis, unknown-prefix fallback, and cost-only warning posture match the predicates and log branches. |\n| 14 | `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py#D:cache_write_never_read` | PASS | The minimum caching-call count and all-write/no-read predicate are exact, while the explanation correctly distinguishes a normal first write from repeated write-only behavior. |\n| 15 | `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py#D:estimate_marked_prefix_tokens` | PASS | Instructions, later message-tail expansion, conservative omission of unavailable tool serialization, `None` fallback, lazy estimator import, and undercounting direction are retained accurately. |\n| 16 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` | PASS | The comment explains why 4096 is the conservative unsourced fallback and correctly identifies both the warm-up and diagnostic consumers of the shared value. |\n| 17 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:_MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` | PASS | The provenance date, direct-Anthropic scope, bare-id normalization, and conservative Bedrock fallback remain explicit beside the per-model table. |\n| 18 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#D:_supports_native_web_search` | PASS | The profile-membership rule mirrors the code and retains provider-independent routing plus conservative `False` behavior for missing dependencies, profiles, or malformed registries. |\n| 19 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#D:web_search_capabilities` | PASS | Provider spelling remains absent from the decision, unflagged calls return `None`, native/local routes stay bounded, missing local grounding fails loudly, and ADR 0063 remains the policy owner. |\n| 20 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:_REBAR_OVERRIDES` | PASS | Ordered first-match family predicates and Claude's prompted-output exception are described without reintroducing provider-name matching, and the Gemini/Groq constraint remains recorded. |\n| 21 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` | PASS | The separation from family defaults, post-family precedence, exact-id non-speculation, temperature exception, and separate regional/global rows match table application. |\n| 22 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:claude-sonnet-4-6` | PASS | The direct Sonnet 4.6 native-output measurement, thinking coverage, bare/provider-qualified normalization, and conservative treatment of unmeasured Claude ids remain clear. |\n| 23 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:claude-opus-4-8` | PASS | The comment accurately explains why the direct Opus row suppresses unsupported temperature before the adapter and avoids claiming deterministic temperature pinning. |\n| 24 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | PASS | Bedrock native structured output under thinking and the continued need for client-side numeric-bound validation remain explicit for the measured rows. |\n| 25 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` | PASS | The dated-profile requirement and bare-alias rejection are retained directly beside the only affected Haiku row. |\n| 26 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:table-close` | PASS | The intentional absence of Bedrock Opus native-output rows is explained by rejection under thinking, preserving the conservative family default rather than implying missing data. |\n| 27 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#C:<module>:before:_GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES` | PASS | Enumerated membership, avoidance of provider-name parsing, and drift-test ownership remain clear at the registry that drives provenance tiering. |\n| 28 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#D:provenance_for` | PASS | The supplied-capability rule, endpoint/gateway tier, unobservable gateway host, effective web route, Bedrock resolver reuse, omitted ambient region, sorted header names, excluded values, and credential-safe hostname extraction all match the record builder. |\n| 29 | `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py#D:cache_settings_for` | PASS | Dispatch remains capability-field-only; instruction/tool marks, multi-turn tail caching, required execution mode, Anthropic/Bedrock key asymmetry, breakpoint bounds, and unchanged single-turn maps are all retained. |\n| 30 | `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The over-150 non-test-line threshold, Gerrit-only scope, accepted `stale-code` and `stale-head`, blocking plan-material states, infrastructure abstention, signer-source policy, and independent Gerrit votes remain explicit. |\n| 31 | `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py#C:<module>:before:_COMPUTE_VALIDITY_VERDICTS` | PASS | The retained vocabulary contains plan-review validity plus local `error`, while correctly excluding completion-only and signer-identity states that cannot reach this criterion. |\n| 32 | `src/rebar/llm/code_review/carry_forward.py#D:<module>` | PASS | Surfaced-and-grounded eligibility, all three region states, ambiguity's fail-safe direction, carry-once termination, Pass 2 isolation, posture clamp, and best-effort sidecar handling remain accurate. |\n| 33 | `src/rebar/llm/code_review/carry_forward.py#D:standing_items` | PASS | The implementation sorts by descending priority, caps the result, uses typed keyspaces, consumes only surfaced findings, requires evidence, records coverage, and catches read or classification failures as documented. |\n| 34 | `src/rebar/llm/completion.py#C:<module>:before:_VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` | PASS | The standard-class default and explicit operator-class precedence are accurately distinguished, with the literal still single-sourced in config. |\n| 35 | `src/rebar/llm/completion.py#C:<module>:before:_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` | PASS | Criteria, child traversal, and fixed overhead remain the scaling inputs, while the separate runaway guards, formula ceiling, and explicit operator budget roles are preserved. |\n| 36 | `src/rebar/llm/completion.py#D:_verifier_model_for_completion` | PASS | Standard-class resolution, parity with plan review, qualified/Bedrock handling, provider-qualified output, repository-root binding, discovery fallback, and test seam all match the helper and its callers. |\n| 37 | `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py#C:<module>:before:NO_VERDICT_CRITERION` | PASS | The comment correctly identifies a framework-owned retryable-fault criterion that leaves the public PASS/FAIL vocabulary unchanged. |\n| 38 | `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py#D:reconcile_verdict` | PASS | Exact-PASS normalization, findings-induced failure, manifest recovery, synthesized no-verdict fault, blocking disposition, framework marker ownership, and idempotent second reconciliation match the branches. |\n| 39 | `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py#C:reconcile_verdict:before:result.pop(verdict_obtainable),occ2` | PASS | The comment accurately narrows marker preservation to the previously synthesized criterion shape and explains why model output cannot gain retryable status through the marker alone. |\n| 40 | `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py#C:reconcile_verdict:before:if verdict == FAIL` | PASS | FAIL-only remediation, framework-derived insufficiency, specialized guidance selection, and PASS cleanup match the following state updates. |\n| 41 | `src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py#D:<module>` | PASS | Private metadata, unchanged schemas, wrapper placement, closure-shared locking, per-response kind assignment, single verdict commit, multi-call evidence response, finite response accounting, and non-governed pass-through remain explicit. |\n| 42 | `src/rebar/llm/config_binding.py#D:<module>` | PASS | Compose-once binding, reentrant instance reuse, explicit-config authority, fail-closed provider/credential composition, pre-call propagation, validated redaction, and review-before-allowlisting are retained. |\n| 43 | `src/rebar/llm/criteria/ids.py#D:<module>` | PASS | Built-in versus `project.<name>` grammar, gate qualification, filesystem-safe conversion, total injective forward mapping, shared consumers, and non-reversibility with hyphens remain exact. |\n| 44 | `src/rebar/llm/criteria/snapshot.py#D:<module>` | PASS | One immutable cross-gate policy snapshot, digest inputs, non-execution ownership, shared applicability, legacy empty-glob behavior, unconditional `**`, and scoped matching remain clear. |\n| 45 | `src/rebar/llm/enrich.py#C:<module>:before:_CONTEXT_CHARS_PER_TOKEN` | PASS | The local conservative conversion remains owned beside its use and explains the dependency reason for not importing the completion workflow onto the store-write path. |\n| 46 | `src/rebar/llm/enrich.py#D:_bound_source` | PASS | The assistance-versus-authoritative evidence boundary, model-window reservation, byte identity, newline-first cut, hard-cut fallback, visible budgeted marker, final bound, and idempotence remain accurate. |\n| 47 | `src/rebar/llm/epic_bug_screen.py#D:<module>` | PASS | The module retains the unresolved open/`in_progress` scope, deterministic `caused_by` floor, temporal/link candidate filter, ceiling, A/B/C meanings, forwarded evidence, degradation policy, systemic-error propagation, audit tally, model class, and cache placement. |\n| 48 | `src/rebar/llm/epic_bug_screen.py#D:_epic_subtree_states` | PASS | The concise contract matches the root-inclusive breadth-first traversal and descendant deduplication immediately below it. |\n| 49 | `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-concurrency.eval.yaml#C:<file>:before:prompt` | PASS | Advisory finding-based scoring, recall/control families, per-epoch deterministic requirements, execution coverage, two-of-three epoch tolerance, R3 non-gating disposition, and offline versus credentialed execution remain documented. |\n| 50 | `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-concurrency.eval.yaml#C:<file>:before:F1-lock-added` | PASS | R3 remains identified as detected drift followed by stale-state use, its non-gating reason and promotion condition remain explicit, and the transition to race-removing controls is clear. |\n| 51 | `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml#C:<file>:before:prompt` | PASS | G3 coverage, G4 sibling consistency, high-confidence scope, negative controls, merged/bin-packed candidate comparison, separate baseline, fidelity dimensions, and offline/CI roles remain explicit. |\n| 52 | `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml#C:<file>:before:tolerance` | PASS | The comment retains the machine-read ownership and the rule that optimization cannot trade away findings or correct G3/G4 attribution; the unchanged numeric fields define the exact margins. |\n\nAggregate: **52 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 CONCERN**.\n\nThe generated `docs/env-vars.md` projection is not an authored allowlist block. Its only change is `bedrock_model.py:78` to `bedrock_model.py:37`, which matches the final source and passes the generator check.\n\n## Stage 1: specification compliance\n\n- Every listed scope location now contains current rationale or constraints: PASS, supported by rows 01 through 52.\n- Every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract remains explicit and accurate: PASS, supported by the corresponding rows above and implementation/caller inspection.\n- No executable behavior, data, test assertion, directive, or non-allowlisted text changed: PASS, supported by normalized AST, protected-comment, directive, and YAML-body comparisons.\n- The generated environment registry matches its generator: PASS.\n- Architecture compliance: PASS. No dependency, interface, state, policy mechanism, or optional-import boundary changed, and the retained dependency descriptions agree with `docs/architecture.md`.\n\nStage 1 verdict: **PASS**.\n\n## Stage 2: documentation quality\n\nThe final prose is materially shorter, current-state oriented, and placed beside the mechanism it explains. It removes ticket narration, incident detail, repeated code narration, and emphasis padding without dropping a scoped invariant. References resolve to existing symbols, configuration, tests, scripts, or ADRs. Authored additions comply with `docs/documentation-policy.md`; the punctuation retained in `docs/env-vars.md` belongs to the generated artifact. I found no critical, important, suggestion, stale, misleading, or recurring issue.\n\nStage 2 verdict: **PASS**.\n\n## Stage 3: domain integrity\n\nThe patch changes no executable type, identifier, validation boundary, state representation, or match behavior. It introduces no primitive domain representation or invalid state. Domain integrity is unchanged.\n\nStage 3 verdict: **PASS**.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Exact `HEAD` and parent: PASS before and after review.\n- Exact 19-path set: PASS.\n- Normalized executable AST and protected-comment comparison: PASS.\n- Directive text and attachment comparison: PASS.\n- Non-allowlisted YAML/body comparison: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`: PASS.\n- `scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`: PASS.\n- `make lint`: PASS.\n- `make typecheck`: PASS.\n- Focused component tests: **360 passed, 1 skipped in 213.56s**.\n- Full repository suite: not run, per the documentation-only epic direction; Gerrit CI owns the full verification contract.\n\n## Review result\n\n```json\n{\n  \"stages\": [\n    {\"stage\": \"spec_compliance\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"findings\": []},\n    {\"stage\": \"code_quality\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"findings\": []},\n    {\"stage\": \"domain_integrity\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"findings\": []}\n  ],\n  \"overall_verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"required_changes_count\": 0,\n  \"blocking_findings_count\": 0,\n  \"receipt_rows\": 52,\n  \"receipt_pass\": 52,\n  \"receipt_fail\": 0\n}\n```\n\nFinal verdict: **PASS**. This exact commit is ready for Gerrit push from the independent documentation-review perspective."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788968182863778001,"uuid":"afbc6e84-118e-4072-abb7-07ddd04e06cb"}